{
  "id": "28422_yugameru",
  "headword": "{歪|ゆが}める",
  "reading": "ゆがめる",
  "romaji": "yugameru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to distort; to twist; to warp",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to distort; to twist; to warp (something)",
      "explanation": "To bend or contort the shape of something out of its normal form. Also used figuratively for distorting facts, expressions, or the truth."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28422_yugameru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{顔|かお}を{歪|ゆが}める。",
      "english": "Twist one's face (in pain or disgust).",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28422_yugameru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{事実|じじつ}を{歪|ゆが}めて{報道|ほうどう}する。",
      "english": "Report the facts in a distorted way.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28422_yugameru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{苦|くる}しさに{口元|くちもと}を{歪|ゆが}め、{何|なに}も{言|い}わずに{立|た}ち{上|あ}がった。",
      "english": "He twisted his mouth in pain and stood up without saying anything.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive ({他動詞|たどうし}). The intransitive pair is {歪|ゆが}む (to become distorted, to warp). Pattern: 〜を{歪|ゆが}める.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {顔|かお}を{歪|ゆが}める: contort one's face (in pain, disgust)\n- {口|くち}を{歪|ゆが}める: twist one's mouth\n- {事実|じじつ}を{歪|ゆが}める: distort the facts\n- {真実|しんじつ}を{歪|ゆが}める: distort the truth\n- {表情|ひょうじょう}を{歪|ゆが}める: contort one's expression\n\nUSAGE:\nIn the literal sense, often describes a facial expression being twisted by strong negative emotion. In the figurative sense, takes abstract objects (facts, history, meaning) and implies dishonesty.",
